{"name":"Indian Ink","hex":"#3c3f4a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"indian","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Indian (“indigene”)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Indian (“indigenous”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indian"},{"term":"ink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pigment (or dye)-based fluid used for writing, printing etc.","A particular type, color or container of this fluid."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply ink to; to cover or smear with ink.","To sign (a contract or similar document)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Indian Ink","blocks":[{"text":"Indian Ink is a 1995 play by Tom Stoppard based on his 1991 radio play In the Native State."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/81/Indian_Ink_Stoppard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_Ink","wikidata":"Q6020553"},{"title":"Indian Ink (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Indian Ink is an Irish-bred British-trained Thoroughbred racehorse and broodmare who was the highest-rated filly trained in the United Kingdom in 2007. As a two-year-old in 2006, she won three of her seven races, culminating in a victory in the Group One Cheveley Park Stakes. In the following year she was beaten in her first two races, but then defeated a strong international field by six lengths to win the Coronation Stakes at Royal Ascot. Throughout her racing career she demonstrated a marked preference for soft ground. At the end of her racing career she was sold for 2,000,000 guineas and retired to stud."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_Ink_(horse)","wikidata":"Q16848225"},{"title":"India ink","blocks":[{"text":"India ink or China ink is a simple black or coloured ink once widely used for writing and printing and now more commonly used for drawing and outlining, especially when inking comic books and comic strips. India ink is also used in medical applications."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/New_Edition_with_Supplemental_Annotations_of_The_Inner_Canon_of_the_Yellow_Emperor._Su_wen_WDL11409.jpg/330px-New_Edition_with_Supplemental_Annotations_of_The_Inner_Canon_of_the_Yellow_Emperor._Su_wen_WDL11409.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India_ink","wikidata":"Q12981547"},{"title":"Ink","blocks":[{"text":"Ink is a gel, sol, or solution that contains at least one colorant, such as a dye or pigment, and is used to color a surface to produce an image, text, or design. Ink is used for drawing or writing with a pen, brush, reed pen, or quill. Thicker inks, in paste form, are used extensively in letterpress and lithographic printing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/F%C3%BCller-tinte_hg.jpg/330px-F%C3%BCller-tinte_hg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ink","wikidata":"Q127418"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Inkstick.jpg/500px-Inkstick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Inkstick.jpg/500px-Inkstick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A solid ink stick used for the preparation of ink","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AInkstick.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Inkmaking_-_Tiangong_Kaiwu.jpg/500px-Inkmaking_-_Tiangong_Kaiwu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Inkmaking_-_Tiangong_Kaiwu.jpg/1280px-Inkmaking_-_Tiangong_Kaiwu.jpg?utm_source=en.